  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Discussion",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Call this endpoint to upload an image that you can associate with a message or a bullet point within the message. You provide a unique `imageIdentifier` to identify each image you upload.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "You can upload image files that meet the following requirements:",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "> **Note**\n>\n> Ensure the images you upload work equally well with both light and dark modes.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The maximum number of images you can configure for each app is 2000. The endpoint returns a `MaximumNumberOfImagesReachedError` response if an attempt to upload an image exceeds this limit. Call `Delete-Image` to delete images.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.retentionmessaging/documentation/RetentionMessaging/Delete-Image"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Use full-size images for a message, or the smaller bullet point-size images to use as bullet points.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": [
        {
          "text": "Format: PNG",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Doesn’t have transparency",
          "refs": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Upload full-size images",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "A full-size image is up to 3840 × 2160 pixels, where the width must be 3840 pixels, and the height can be between 160 to 2160 pixels.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "You can add alternative text for images when you call `Upload-Message` and associate an image with a message using `UploadMessageImage`.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.retentionmessaging/documentation/RetentionMessaging/Upload-Message",
            "doc://com.apple.retentionmessaging/documentation/RetentionMessaging/UploadMessageImage"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Upload images for bullet points",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Images you use for bullet points are 1024 x 1024 pixels. You can add alternative text for the bullet point images when you supply `bulletPoints` in the `UploadMessageRequestBody`.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.retentionmessaging/documentation/RetentionMessaging/UploadMessageRequestBody"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "> **Note**\n>\n> This endpoint isn’t idempotent. If you attempt to upload an image and reuse a previously configured `imageIdentifier`, the endpoint returns the `ImageAlreadyExistsError` response.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.retentionmessaging/documentation/RetentionMessaging/ImageAlreadyExistsError"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Determine whether an image is ready to display",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Immediately after you upload an image, its `imageState` is `PENDING`. Apple checks the images, and sets the image state to `APPROVED` to indicate the system can display them in retention messaging. Call the `Get-Image-List` endpoint to check the current state of images you upload.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.retentionmessaging/documentation/RetentionMessaging/imageState",
            "doc://com.apple.retentionmessaging/documentation/RetentionMessaging/Get-Image-List"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the sandbox testing environment, the system automatically sets the message and image states to `APPROVED`.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    }
  ],
